# The project's pre-commit checks.
#
# git_hooks runs this file inside the workspace's container, so every
# line here is a command of the project, not of your machine: `mix`,
# not `docker compose exec`. Run them yourself, without committing,
# with `sh .githooks/pre-commit`.
#
# Each cartridge owns a block, delimited by its name. Yours go outside
# them, or in a block of your own: a cartridge only ever rewrites the
# block it opened, and takes it away when it is ejected. Moving a block
# is how you reorder the checks — it is replaced where it stands, never
# put back where it was born.
#
# The first failure stops the commit. `git commit --no-verify` skips
# the lot, which is what a hook is: a reminder that runs for the person
# who installed it, never a gate.
